--- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $30$ | $26$ | $1$ | ? | $3$ | $12$ | $28$ |" :question/worked-solution "A rule is a function if and only if every input is mapped to *precisely one* output.\n\n- If we substitute the $xy$-pair $(3,2)$ into our table, we get a function.\n\n| **$x$** | $-6$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $4$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $30$ | $26$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $12$ | $28$ |\n\nNotice that all values in the first row are *distinct* (i.e., different). Every input value is assigned to *precisely one* output value.\n\n- None of the other $xy$-pairs gives rules that are functions. So, for example, substituting the $xy$-pair $(4,12)$ gives a rule that is *not* a function. \n\n| **$x$** | $-6$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $4$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $30$ | $26$ | $1$ | $12$ | $3$ | $12$ | $28$ |\n\nNotice that the first row contains the value $x=4$ twice. The input value $4$ is assigned to *more than one* output value ($3$ and $12$)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078527 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cc2167e-d318-54d5-8b67-47afbc65f530" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Rule Given by a Mapping Diagram Is a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cad4dd8-ca6d-55ab-9dc5-081de80e69a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Not enough information" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077655} {:answer/id #uuid "001094b5-522b-5aff-87d8-cdfd551294ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No, since there is at least one output with more than one input" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077656} {:answer/id #uuid "3024a1e1-3c8f-5f6d-ab79-bde1c13d5709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since each input is assigned to exactly one output" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077657} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd5fdb7-c2a9-539d-b5b1-60da0e4d051a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since each output is related to at least one input" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077658} {:answer/id #uuid "6008c3f2-d2aa-5fd1-96b6-5ae4ce87bd88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No, since both sets have different numbers of elements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3024a1e1-3c8f-5f6d-ab79-bde1c13d5709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since each input is assigned to exactly one output" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077657} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d9b076-e24e-5725-bd8f-2293f79ac91a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77dee980-a89b-544a-9fab-994ab35aaa5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-60621" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aaba52792efd52cae40bed740b50f3f92f54e0f13436c16ffc8358ff8200cd76.png)\n\nIs the above rule a function?" :question/worked-solution "A rule is a function if and only if *every* input is mapped to *precisely one* output.\n\nIn particular, a rule is *not* a function in the following cases:\n\n- An input value is not assigned to an output value. For example, the following situation is *not allowed* for functions (an input value with no arrow from it):\n\n![](images/bb/bb53865d210d631d78e5ce48aa96ecff99da8995936a085c789c3471ffb9e6a0.png)\n\n \n\n- An input value is assigned to more than one output value. For example, the following situation is *not allowed* for functions (an input value with more than one arrow from it):\n\n![](images/18/18831dc73e561faa69748fed111eb7e1024d35849fb6624594ae08d8c35301ee.png)\n\n \n\nIn this particular example, the rule *is* a function because *each* input value is assigned *precisely one* output value."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078527 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cc2167e-d318-54d5-8b67-47afbc65f530" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Rule Given by a Mapping Diagram Is a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b452610-1a90-593f-89a8-1c4334f8692e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since both sets have the same number of elements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509841} {:answer/id #uuid "a9162203-d658-5d42-9df6-3ec42dbfef2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since each output is related to at least one input" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510049} {:answer/id #uuid "c10dd595-c5fb-5d9b-b6ec-8500d9d83c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since each input is assigned to exactly one output" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510092} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc3a002-b6d3-5418-8801-26229653dddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Not enough information" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510122} {:answer/id #uuid "e849c16f-4c33-5f1d-9015-49309af959d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No, since both sets have the same number of elements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c10dd595-c5fb-5d9b-b6ec-8500d9d83c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Yes, since each input is assigned to exactly one output" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510092} :answer-field/id #uuid "0509729a-0cf8-5abe-9a21-a913a1bfda28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f8427f7-1892-52e0-9e03-33a7a2709f34" :question/math-academy-id "q-6728" :question/problem "![](images/99/998d9b7d5d9e342f58add32f80cddfcb6f01e255497f87376c0e39e01abb67ba.png)\n\nIs the above rule a function?" :question/worked-solution "A rule is a function if and only if *every* input is mapped to *precisely one* output.\n\nIn particular, a rule is *not* a function in the following cases:\n\n- An input value is not assigned to an output value. For example, the following situation is *not allowed* for functions (an input value with no arrow from it):\n\n![](images/bb/bb53865d210d631d78e5ce48aa96ecff99da8995936a085c789c3471ffb9e6a0.png)\n\n \n\n- An input value is assigned to more than one output value. For example, the following situation is *not allowed* for functions (an input value with more than one arrow from it):\n\n![](images/18/18831dc73e561faa69748fed111eb7e1024d35849fb6624594ae08d8c35301ee.png)\n\n \n\nIn this particular example, the rule *is* a function because *each* input value is assigned *precisely one* output value."}]}
